body:
I emailed support to ask why macOS version doesn&#39;t sync and was told:
&#34;We are so sorry for your bad experience with Habitify. Since the update version is only released on phone, not the MacOS yet, it causes the issue about the synchronization among platforms. Our developer team is working on completing Habitify on all other platforms as soon as possible. Meanwhile, I hope you can use the mobile app and web app for a better experience. If you have any problem, please let me know.&#34;

There is another review her from May sayign the same thing. They&#39;re selling a premium product whic proports to sync on their website and that&#39;s a main feature/benefit of paying and they know it doesn&#39;t work. The app is ok other than that not great but the abovei is just straight up false advertising.

Yet another promising looking app that you can download for free but hits you with, &#34;Pay X amount to access our premium features!&#34; 
I will say at least this app is a one time fee unlike a lot of apps lately that expect people to pay a monthly fee to use premium features. 
However, the free version only lets you track ONE habit. ONE. If you expect people to pay $6 to make this app even somewhat useful you should offer a better sample of what people will be getting when they buy. Maybe allow free users to track 3 habits (one for morning, afternoon, and evenjng or whatever the person chooses).
